on.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-c6a"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-c6a"],"id":"long.record-257bm-c6a","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.73 (Two consecutive skips)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.73, p. 65, label record:257bm-c6a","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*If $c\\ge6$ and the real half-greedy rule skips both $c$ and $c+1$, put $D=G\\cap\\{2,\\ldots,c-1\\}$. Then\n$$\nS(D,1,2c-3)<2^{c-3}.\n$$\nThe one-step quotient recurrence gives $S(D,1,2c-2)<2^{c-2}$, so Theorem 6.75 supplies an exact row at depth $2c-2$ whose new ranks are all greater than $c$. The hypothesis concerns this pair of skipped ranks; no unbounded sequence of such pairs is proved here. For the stated precritical-suffix condition at every skipped rank, the remaining tests are the skip-then-take cases, with ranks $4$ and $5$ handled separately in the cited proof.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-c6a","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-c6a","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c6a%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfGreedySkippedCriticalQuotientSupply%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c6a%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfGreedySkippedCriticalQuotientSupply%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.HalfGreedySkippedCriticalQuotientSupply"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-c6a","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1